{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["And the meaning of <b>and the waters prevailed</b> — <b>the waters prevailed</b> — is that they multiplied greatly, for to a great increase the language of גבורה is applied, as in \"and their transgression when they grow strong\" (Job 36:9) — they multiplied greatly; \"great is His kindness toward those who fear Him\" (Psalms 103:11) — it is great; and likewise \"and if in strong [years] eighty years\" (Psalms 90:10) — in a great increase. And it is possible that the meaning of \"prevailed\" is that the waters came in a torrent and uprooted the trees and toppled the buildings, for to force the term גבורה is applied, because גבורה is in strength, as in \"even they grow strong in power\" (Job 21:7), \"and he will make firm a covenant with the many for one week\" (Daniel 9:27) — he will establish it firmly. And the language of the Sages (Ta'anit 2a): \"the גבורה of rains,\" is because they come down with force. And it is possible that from this sense comes \"and if in strong [years] eighty years\" — that if his bones and body were strong and he was a man of strength, he would live eighty years. If so, the meaning of \"they prevailed upon the earth\" would be that in their force they covered everything, even the high mountains, and swept them away."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:26:00.592724358Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}